From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:14:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] milkflint tests: run clean under KASAN, lockdep and kmemleak

A KUnit kernel with KASAN, UBSAN, lockdep and kmemleak found these in
the tests themselves; the driver code they call was right each time:

- mt76-agg-rx compared all of jiffies with the 32-bit reorder_time,
  which agg-rx.c compares as 32 bits (time_before32()): the check
  fails once jiffies passes 2^32, five minutes after boot.
- mt76-eeprom stripped the device's OF nodes in a kunit action
  registered after the nodes' own, so it ran after their release and
  walked freed memory. It's the suite's exit now, which runs first.
- mt76_test_reset_device's second band had no tx_lock set up, which
  registering it does (mt76_phy_init()).
- mt76_test_dfs_state_cac checked a radar channel without the wiphy
  mutex that cfg80211 asserts there; mac80211 holds it when it calls
  the driver.
- The fake's register xarray took its lock with interrupts on, while
  the irq tasklet and code under the driver's irq_lock write registers
  too. It takes it with interrupts off now.
- Tests called softirq-path code with BH on, or without the rx poll's
  RCU read section: the txwi cache, tx_queue_skb(), txwi_free() and
  mt7915_mac_tx_free(). They call it as the driver does now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/tests/mac-test.c |  9 ++++++
 tests/agg-rx-test.c     |  4 ++-
 tests/connac-mac-test.c | 22 ++++++++++++++
 tests/core-test.c       |  6 ++++
 tests/dma-test.c        | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 tests/eeprom-test.c     | 14 ++++++---
 tests/fake.h            | 10 ++++--
 tests/record-test.c     |  2 +-
 8 files changed, 109 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
index 15ab5c12..0b77385b 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/mac-test.c
@@ -214,7 +214,12 @@ static void mt7915_test_tx_free_short_event(struct kunit *test)
 	struct mt7915_dev *dev = mt7915_test_tx_dev(test);
 	u8 ev[4] = {};
 
+	/* as the rx poll runs it: BH off, RCU read section */
+	local_bh_disable();
+	rcu_read_lock();
 	mt7915_mac_tx_free(dev, ev, sizeof(ev));
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+	local_bh_enable();
 
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt7915_test_cleanups, 0);
 }
@@ -235,7 +240,11 @@ static void mt7915_test_tx_free_truncated_event(struct kunit *test)
 	ev.info[0] = cpu_to_le32(FIELD_PREP(MT_TX_FREE_MSDU_ID, 5));
 	q->blocked = true;
 
+	local_bh_disable();
+	rcu_read_lock();
 	mt7915_mac_tx_free(dev, &ev, sizeof(ev));
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+	local_bh_enable();
 
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, q->blocked);
 }
